course: dictionary
lesson: 12204
title: Confucianism: a way of living
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Confucianism is a way of thinking and living that comes from the teachings of Confucius, a Chinese teacher who lived about 2,500 years ago. It teaches people to be kind, honest and polite, and to respect their parents and elders. «In our religious education lesson we studied Confucianism, Daoism and Buddhism.» Here it is a subject that people learn about.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «Mei's family lives by Confucian values, so she always helps her grandmother and says thank you.» Confucian values means values that come from Confucius's teachings, such as kindness and respect. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Confucius was a Chinese teacher who lived about 2,500 years ago.
fact: Confucianism stresses kindness, honesty, good manners, education and respect for parents, elders and rulers.
fact: «Filial piety» means respect and care for your parents.
fact: The Golden Rule in Confucianism is: «Do not do to others what you would not want done to yourself.»
fact: Many people see Confucianism more as a philosophy of good behaviour than as a religion with a god.
exercise: «The teachings of Confucius are studied in our history lesson.» Who was Confucius? | *A Chinese teacher who lived about 2,500 years ago | A king who ruled a country in Europe | A footballer from Korea | A Roman general
exercise: «Filial piety» means what? | *Respect and care for your parents | Playing music loudly at home | Eating together every Sunday | Winning every race at sports day
exercise: Which idea is the Golden Rule in Confucianism? | Only trust people you have known for years | Keep your bedroom tidy at all times | *Do not do to others what you would not want done to yourself | Always win every game you play
test: Ming says Confucianism is a religion with a god, just like the others. Which is closer to the truth? | *Many people see it more as a way of good behaviour than as a religion with a god | It is a kind of Chinese noodle dish | It is a sport played in schools | Yes, it has one god who made the world
test: «Her family lives by Confucian values.» What do Confucian values most likely mean? | *Kindness, honesty, good manners and respect for elders | Rules about football matches | Only speaking loudly at dinner | Living in a castle on a hill
exam: In Confucianism, what does «ren» mean? | Keeping secrets from your family | Reading the newspaper every day | *Kindness to others | Being the fastest runner in the class
